      "id": 1,
      "text": "Edgewood began as a shipping depot on the Texas and Pacific railroad in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://edgewoodtexas.org/about-us/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original settlement, called Barren Ridge, was founded two miles southeast of today’s Edgewood along the Dallas–Shreveport road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://edgewoodtexas.org/about-us/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1920s Edgewood grew to include a canning plant, a broom factory, and a basket factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/edgewood-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1976 the Edgewood Historical Society opened Heritage Park Museum, preserving 21 restored structures that showcase rural East Texas culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
